> if I had all those, is there anything I'm really missing for an ascension
> kit? maybe add a =oConflict, or such?  any suggestions?

=oConflict is nice, and lots of people seem to want =oFreeAction. You 
want a blessed unicorn horn of course. If you want to keep a pet, a 
magic whistle is nice, and some source of light is good to have as well. 
You already had a means of levitation. Other than that, some useful 
items are:

* holy water, lots of it, when going into Gehennom
* some means of escape: ?oTele, /oTele (also for teleporting away 
monsters), /oDig
* food; most people go with K-rations, since they have the highest 
nutrition/weight ratio, and only take one turn to eat
* wand or scroll of fire (slime)
* some means of healing
* some means of locking/unlocking doors
* some means of blinding yourself, if you have telepathy
* some kind of long range weapon: daggers, arrows etc, or a spell or wands
* some way of digging

I've probably forgotten something, there's just so much useful stuff. I 
guess I'll always need a BoH :)

> Also, I'm thinking of doing wizards for a while, so as far as they go, the
> ascension kit would be similar except with GoDex and HoB right? or can they
> not effectively use SDSM?

With wizards, you should take care not to hinder spellcasting, 
especially not in the early game. So no metal, and no shields. And 
you'll use spells more, so weapons will be less important. But I'm no 
expert on wizards, so I'll leave this to others.

